  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Ukraine - Support to Civilians in Conflict &#xbf; Conflict Monitoring, Community-Based Warning Systems, and Promotion of Humanitarian Law</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This 18-month measure aims to support the protection of civilians in Ukraine as well as work towards ensuring that further escalation can be prevented and the perpetrators of war crimes and crimes against humanity can ultimately be held to account, and missing persons located.A first component of the action will focus on practical solutions to effectively preserve and archive information and evidence of violations of international humanitarian law, and to enable communities to better anticipate and avoid harm to civilians from military operations. This will involve the urgent deployment and implementation of innovative information technology to&amp;nbsp;identify, preserve, and archive information and evidence of international crimes in close cooperation with local civil society groups and for use in investigations by national and international justice actors, including the Office of the Prosecutor General of Ukraine, International Criminal Court or the Office of the High Commissioner for Human rights and related bodies. The component will also include the deployment of mobile-phone based reporting systems for use by civilians in Ukraine to warn of imminent life threatening danger to their communities, in close cooperation with the relevant Ukrainian Civil Protection Authorities. A second component of the action will support Ukraine&#xbf;s efforts in recording and tracing of persons who go missing thereby enabling the responsible State Authorities to track disappearances during the war and providing evidence to relevant international justice authorities. A third component will focus on the promotion and awareness raising of international humanitarian law, as well as on the obligations arising from this, including in regards to the principled delivery of humanitarian assistance and the facilitation of humanitarian access. This will involve in person awareness raising sessions where possible, as well as tailor made IT-supported campaigning, adapted to reaching military actors under the command of both conflicting parties as well as the civilian population.</narrative>
  </description>
